---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
---

<Layout 
  title="Disclaimer - Educational Settlement Models | FreeInjuryCalc"
  description="Read the legal disclaimer of FreeInjuryCalc.com. Understand that our online settlement calculators do not provide formal legal advice."
>
  <Header />

  <main class="flex-grow bg-canvas transition-colors duration-200 py-16 md:py-24 animate-fade-in">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 font-sans">
      
      <!-- Page Header -->
      <div class="border-b border-hairline pb-8 mb-12">
        <span class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-link font-mono bg-link-bg-soft/30 dark:bg-link-bg-soft/10 px-3 py-1 rounded-full">
          Legal Safeguards
        </span>
        <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-ink mt-4 mb-4">
          Disclaimer
        </h1>
        <p class="text-sm md:text-base text-body leading-relaxed">
          Last updated: June 10, 2026. Please read this disclaimer carefully before relying on any estimations generated by FreeInjuryCalc.com.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Content -->
      <div class="space-y-8 text-xs md:text-sm text-body leading-relaxed">
        
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-lg md:text-xl font-bold text-ink">1. Educational & Illustrative Models Only</h2>
          <p>
            All mathematical calculations, dollar figures, and settlement ranges generated by FreeInjuryCalc.com (including state-specific car accident calculators, whiplash calculators, back/neck injury calculators, workers' comp benefits calculators, and diminished value calculators) are intended strictly for educational and illustrative purposes. 
          </p>
          <p>
            These results represent automated mathematical modeling based on user inputs and generic statistical formulas (such as the standard 1.5x–5x medical bill multiplier or the 17c diminished value cap). They do not reflect the actual, guaranteed settlement value of any real personal injury claim.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-4 p-6 border border-hairline bg-canvas-soft-2 rounded-lg">
          <h3 class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-ink font-mono mb-2">No Attorney-Client Relationship</h3>
          <p class="text-[11px] leading-relaxed">
            Your use of this website, its calculator modules, contact forms, or communication emails does not create an attorney-client relationship between you and FreeInjuryCalc, its developers, or its editorial board. None of the contents written on this platform constitute formal legal representation, advocacy, or advice.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-lg md:text-xl font-bold text-ink">2. Realities of Insurance Claims Valuations</h2>
          <p>
            In the real world, insurance companies (such as State Farm, Progressive, GEICO, and Allstate) do not evaluate bodily injury claims using simple, public-facing multipliers. Instead, they rely on proprietary claims assessment software systems (like <strong>Colossus</strong> or <strong>TEACH</strong>). 
          </p>
          <p>
            These software programs evaluate claims by processing highly granular inputs, including medical billing codes, diagnostic proof (e.g. objective MRI scans showing herniated discs vs. subjective soft-tissue neck stiffness), duration of treatment gaps, geographic venue, and the defense attorney's trial record. Consequently, actual insurance offers may be significantly lower or higher than the calculations generated by our automated tool.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-lg md:text-xl font-bold text-ink">3. Limitation of Liability</h2>
          <p>
            Under no circumstances will FreeInjuryCalc, its parent entities, developers, or legal editors be held liable for any decisions made, actions taken, or losses incurred in reliance on the calculations or contents of this website. If you are negotiating an active insurance claim, you assume full responsibility for your actions. We strongly recommend hiring a licensed, practicing personal injury attorney in your state or province to receive a personalized evaluation of your case.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
